# Third-party notices

Peephole itself is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE). It declares **no third-party module
dependencies**: `go.mod` has no `require` directives and there is no `go.sum`
(`go list -deps ./...` reports 120 packages — 3 our own, 117 Go standard library,
0 third-party). There is no vendored source tree and no file in this repository
carries a foreign copyright header.

The distributed artifacts in `bin/` and on the GitHub releases page are
statically-linked Go binaries, so they contain object code from the Go standard
library. The Go licence is BSD-3-Clause, whose clause 2 requires that
redistributions in binary form reproduce its copyright notice. That notice is
reproduced in full below to satisfy that condition.

No other third-party material is redistributed. The wordmark and logo in `assets/`
are original SVG path artwork with no embedded fonts and no external references.

